The Gear meta check's fixture: set/ is a tree of recipes, filed the way
ports/core files them, in which every Gear application no other port depends
on is named by exactly one kde-gear-* meta. dolphin and libkdegames are named
by none and pass, because dolphin-plugins and the games depend on them and
bring them in; the Frameworks are no Gear family's. testing/preflight.sh
checks that set/ passes, then copies it twice: once with kapman dropped from
kde-gear-games, which must fail as named by no meta, and once with bovo added
to kde-gear-core, which must fail as named by two.
